.TH CADO 1 "August 23, 2026" "VirtualSquare Labs"
.SH NAME
cado \- execute a command with authorized ambient capabilities
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cado
[
.I options
]
.I capability-list
[
.I command
[
.I args ...
]
]
.br
.B cado -v
.br
.B cado -s
[
.B -v
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cado
delegates selected Linux ambient capabilities without changing the command to a
root identity. Authorization is read from
.BR cado.conf (5).
For ordinary execution, PAM authenticates the current user after authorization
and after cado drops its setuid identity.
.PP
.I capability-list
is a comma-separated list of libcap names, with or without the
.B cap_
prefix, or unsigned unprefixed hexadecimal masks. Field-edge whitespace is
ignored. Empty items, signs, overflow, trailing text, unsupported bits, and an
empty list are errors.
.PP
If
.I command
is omitted, cado executes
.BR $SHELL .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -f , " --force"
Grant the intersection of requested and authorized capabilities. Without this
option, any unavailable requested bit denies execution.
.TP
.BR -v , " --verbose"
Print capability sets. Used alone, list the capabilities authorized for the
current identity.
.TP
.BR -S , " --scado"
Require an explicit absolute command path and a matching per-user scado entry.
No PAM prompt is made. A persisted digest causes cado to execute a protected,
verified copy while preserving the original command as
.IR argv[0] .
.TP
.BR -s , " --setcap"
As root, compute and apply cado's minimum file capability set from the complete
configuration plus
.BR cap_dac_read_search .
This mode accepts no command or capability operands and is incompatible with
.B -f
and
.BR -S .
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print usage and exit.
.SH SECURITY MODEL
The installed cado executable is setuid to the unprivileged
.B _cado
account rather than UID 0. Its file capabilities are limited to configured
delegations plus the capability needed to read protected configuration and scado
files. Condition children drop ambient capabilities.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cado.conf (5),
.BR scado (1),
.BR cadrop (1),
.BR caprint (1),
.BR capabilities (7)
